{"tool_calls": [{"id": "toolu_bdrk_01KS6awqyUm1X8t6qMH8KWdX", "name": "file_read", "arguments": {"file_path": "summary/CPI_offsite_construction_SCM_summary.json"}}]}成功执行，结果为tool_result:{"status": "success", "output": "{
  "content": "{\n  \"title\": \"Cyber-physical internet based intelligent operation platform for off-site construction supply chain management\",\n  \"authors\": [\"Li Yin\", \"Tengda Li\", \"Guojin Li\", \"Svetlana Besklubova\", \"Ray Y. Zhong\", \"Shuxuan Zhao\"],\n  \"publication_info\": \"Enterprise Information Systems, 2024, VOL. 18, NO. 6, 771-794\",\n  \"sections\": {\n    \"abstract\": {\n      \"summary\": \"The paper proposes a three-layered cyber-physical internet (CPI)-based platform for off-site construction supply chain management (OSC-SCM). The platform includes a scalable layer connecting resources via industrial drivers, a kernel layer with digital twin protocols and information sharing mechanisms, and an application layer offering thirteen services for off-site plants, logistics, and on-site assembly. A case study demonstrated 20% reduced construction time and significant cost savings.\"\n    },\n    \"introduction\": {\n      \"summary\": \"Prefabricated buildings are gaining popularity globally but present challenges in supply chain management. Previous studies have focused on separate stages of the supply chain, with identified research gaps in business flow integration and application of CPI technology. The paper introduces CPI as an interconnected network infrastructure that enables seamless integration between physical objects and digital systems, with Digital Twins (DTs) playing a key role in realizing this vision.\"\n    },\n    \"literature_review\": {\n      \"summary\": \"The literature review covers three main areas: (1) Off-site construction supply chain management, which is critical due to the complexity and fragmentation of logistics in OSC; (2) Cyber-physical systems in supply chain management, which can establish connections between BIM models and on-site assembly sensors; and (3) Digital Twin technology in construction, which offers benefits throughout the entire lifecycle of construction projects from design to demolition.\"\n    },\n    \"platform_framework\": {\n      \"summary\": \"The proposed CPI-OSCSCM platform consists of three layers: (1) The scalable access layer connects diverse stakeholders through industrial drivers and integrated information chains; (2) The kernel services layer includes twin protocols, networking modules, incentive mechanisms, and secure sharing functionalities; (3) The application layer supports different aspects of off-site plant operations, logistics processes, and on-site assembly.\"\n    },\n    \"scalable_access_layer\": {\n      \"summary\": \"This layer integrates stakeholders through a 'plug and play' approach using industrial drivers that enable identification and organization of resources. The integrated information chains provide specifications for data exchange among logistics stakeholders, with a meta-data graph structure containing nodes (representing entities), edges (describing relationships), and global information.\"\n    },\n    \"kernel_services_layer\": {\n      \"summary\": \"This layer includes: (1) Twin protocols defining communication rules at static, dynamic, and prediction levels; (2) Kernel services providing data services, data weaving, function services, and algorithm capabilities; (3) Incentive mechanisms for DT partnerships including revenue sharing, cost sharing, performance-based incentives, intellectual property sharing, and reputational benefits; (4) Information sharing mechanisms based on digital identity management.\"\n    },\n    \"application_layer\": {\n      \"summary\": \"The application layer covers three main areas: (1) Off-site plant applications including design and planning, production and manufacturing, quality control, and maintenance; (2) Logistics process applications including transport route planning, status monitoring, load layout optimization, cost analysis, and PC traceability; (3) On-site assembly applications including safety monitoring, construction process management, stakeholder collaboration, and on-site logistics optimization.\"\n    },\n    \"case_study\": {\n      \"summary\": \"The case study focused on a high-rise construction project in Hubei Province, China, with 270,000 square meters of construction area. The project addressed challenges in information synchronization among stakeholders, logistics management, and construction of prefabricated components. The implementation demonstrated improved production efficiency (13.7%), reduced construction time (20%), and cost savings of millions of CNY.\"\n    },\n    \"conclusion\": {\n      \"summary\": \"The paper proposed a CPI platform with three layers to support OSC supply chain operations. The platform enhances visibility, control, and optimization through Digital Twins and twin networks. Future research will explore blockchain technology for data sharing, focus on data security, and expand case studies for system testing and evaluation.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"key_findings\": [\n    \"The three-layered CPI platform improved construction efficiency by 13.7% and reduced construction time by 20%\",\n    \"The platform ensured 100% visibility and traceability of project resources\",\n    \"Implementation resulted in significant cost savings of approximately 3.5 million CNY\",\n    \"The platform improved information granularity management through hierarchical standardization\",\n    \"Digital Twins technology enabled effective simulation, monitoring, and optimization of the supply chain\"\n  ],\n  \"key_technologies\": [\n    \"Cyber-Physical Internet (CPI)\",\n    \"Digital Twin (DT) technology\",\n    \"Industrial drivers for stakeholder integration\",\n    \"Meta-data graph structures for information chains\",\n    \"Digital identity management for secure information sharing\"\n  ],\n  \"research_gaps_addressed\": [\n    \"Integration of business flow alongside material and information flows in OSC-SCM\",\n    \"Application of CPI technology to foster cooperation among stakeholders across multiple stages\"\n  ],\n  \"future_work\": [\n    \"Exploration of blockchain technology for stakeholder data sharing\",\n    \"Enhancing data security through improved stakeholder collaboration\",\n    \"Expanding case studies for robust system testing and evaluation\"\n  ]\n}",
